<http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/assertion> {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-bilayer-curvature> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-bilayer-curvature> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Bilayer curvature from differential swelling (Timoshenko)" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-bilayer-curvature> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A thin two-layer strip whose layers swell by different amounts bends with a uniform curvature proportional to the swelling-strain mismatch, with a geometric coefficient fixed by the thickness ratio and modulus ratio of the layers; the pine cone scale is such a bilayer, its outer (active) sclerenchyma layer swelling along the scale and its inner (passive) layer not." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-bilayer-curvature> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/TestableHypothesis> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-bilayer-curvature> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "\\kappa = \\frac{6(1+m)^2}{h\\,[3(1+m)^2 + (1+mn)(m^2 + 1/(mn))]}\\,\\Delta\\varepsilon, \\quad m = h_1/h_2,\\ n = E_1/E_2,\\ h = h_1+h_2; \\text{ for } m = 1, n = 1: \\kappa = \\tfrac{3}{2}\\,\\Delta\\varepsilon / h" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-bilayer-curvature> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Assumptions: linear elasticity, Euler–Bernoulli kinematics (plane sections, slender strip, w/L << 1), perfect bonding at the interface, uniform eigenstrain in each layer, small strains. Formal status: proved; this is Timoshenko's 1925 bimetal-thermostat result with thermal strain replaced by hygroscopic strain, which Reyssat and Mahadevan (2009) apply to pine cone scales and biomimetic paper–polymer bilayers. Whether a real scale's layers satisfy the assumptions (uniform, well-bonded, linearly elastic, slender) is empirical." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-bilayer-curvature> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/proposedTest> "Measure, on pine cone scales, the thickness of the active and passive layers, their Young's moduli, and the swelling strain of the active layer between dry and wet states; compute the predicted curvature change and compare it with the measured curvature change of the same scales (Reyssat & Mahadevan 2009, Fig. 2; Quan et al. 2021 give layer thicknesses, moduli and deformation for Pinus scales). Pass if predicted and measured curvature agree within the measurement uncertainty, or at least within a factor of two with the right ordering across specimens." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-bilayer-curvature> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hypothesisType> "model-theorem" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-bilayer-curvature> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Etienne Reyssat & L. Mahadevan (2009) Hygromorphs: from pine cones to biomimetic bilayers" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-bilayer-curvature> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://doi.org/10.1364/JOSA.11.000233> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-bilayer-curvature> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://doi.org/10.1038/37745> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-bilayer-curvature> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.actbio.2021.04.049> .
}
